      thumbnail: nlpThumb,
  
      overview: 'Mid-exam project for the Natural Language Processing (NLP) in Healthcare course at President University. The project builds a complete NLP pipeline for multi-class medical text classification on the MedQuad dataset — 16,407 medical Q&A pairs sourced from 9 NIH-affiliated organizations (GHR, GARD, CDC, CancerGov, NHLBI, NIDDK, NIHSeniorHealth, NINDS, MPlusHealthTopics). The pipeline covers missing value handling, custom text preprocessing, TF-IDF feature engineering, NMF topic modeling for latent theme discovery, and a head-to-head comparison of Multinomial Naive Bayes vs Logistic Regression classifiers evaluated via stratified 80/20 split.',
  
      problem: 'The MedQuad dataset presents three compounded challenges: (1) significant class imbalance — GHR and GARD together exceed 60% of records while CDC represents only 1.6%, creating majority-class bias risk where naive accuracy hides poor minority-class recall; (2) unstructured long-form medical text requiring multi-step normalization before vectorization can proceed without runtime errors; (3) high-dimensional sparse TF-IDF representation with up to 2,000 features requiring careful dimensionality management to avoid the Curse of Dimensionality while preserving discriminative medical terminology.',
  
      solution: 'A structured 9-step NLP pipeline implemented in a single Jupyter notebook: drop 5 NaN rows from the `answer` column → apply `clean_text` (lowercase + regex + NLTK stopwords) → TfidfVectorizer(max_features=2000) producing (16407×2000) sparse matrix → NMF(n_components=5) for topic discovery → stratified 80/20 split (stratify=y, 13125 train / 3282 test) → train MultinomialNB and LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000) → evaluate with accuracy_score, classification_report, and Seaborn confusion matrix heatmaps.',
  
      solutionCards: [
        { title: 'MedQuad Dataset', desc: '16,407 medical Q&A records from 9 NIH sources. 5 missing answer rows dropped. Class imbalance: GHR/GARD >60%, CDC=1.6%. Stratified split preserves proportions.' },
        { title: 'Text Preprocessing', desc: 'clean_text pipeline: lowercase → re.sub(r\'[^a-zA-Z\\s]\') removes numbers/symbols → NLTK English stopwords removal → improves Signal-to-Noise Ratio for medical terms.' },
        { title: 'TF-IDF + NMF', desc: 'TfidfVectorizer(max_features=2000) → (16407, 2000) sparse matrix. NMF (5 components) uncovers: Topic 2 (genetics: gene, autosomal, recessive) and Topic 5 (chronic: blood, cancer, treatment, heart).' },
        { title: 'Model Comparison', desc: 'Multinomial Naive Bayes: 79.49% accuracy, macro F1=0.753. Logistic Regression (max_iter=1000): 90.80% accuracy, macro F1=0.869. LR wins by +11.3 percentage points.' },
      ],
  
      architecture: 'Single Jupyter notebook pipeline: (1) Import libraries (Pandas, NumPy, NLTK, scikit-learn, Matplotlib, Seaborn) → (2) pd.set_option display config → (3) pd.read_csv("medquad.csv") → df.dropna(subset=["answer","source"]) → 16,407 clean records → (4) source_counts bar chart (DistributionOfSources) → (5) clean_text: .lower() + re.sub(r"[^a-zA-Z\\s]") + NLTK stopword filter → df["answer_clean"] → (6) TfidfVectorizer(max_features=2000).fit_transform → X_tfidf (16407, 2000) → (7) NMF(n_components=5) → topic-word matrix H, doc-topic matrix W → keywords DataFrame → (8) train_test_split(test_size=0.2, stratify=y) → 13125/3282 → (9) MultinomialNB + LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000) → accuracy + classification_report + confusion_matrix Seaborn heatmaps.',
  
      architectureTags: ['MedQuad', 'TF-IDF', 'NMF Topic Modeling', 'Multinomial Naive Bayes', 'Logistic Regression', 'Stratified Split', 'NLTK Stopwords', 'Confusion Matrix'],
  
