      conclusion: 'The NLP pipeline successfully classifies MedQuad medical answer texts into their 9 source categories, with Logistic Regression achieving 90.80% accuracy and macro F1=0.869 — outperforming Multinomial Naive Bayes (79.49%, macro F1=0.753) by 11.3 percentage points. The result confirms that discriminative models with L2 regularization outperform generative models on high-dimensional TF-IDF feature spaces where medical word co-occurrence violates the Naive Bayes independence assumption. NMF topic modeling successfully identifies 5 coherent latent themes, with the genetic disorder topic (gene, autosomal, recessive) directly explaining the GHR/GARD source dominance pattern. The stratified split strategy preserved CDC minority-class representation (1.6%) in evaluation, ensuring reliable macro-average metrics.',
